+# Astra review 7741 — rebind-journal reset durability and recovery
+
+## Verdict: NOT APPROVED
+
+Reviewed **`2c7e337202cbfa19569b344992326a1603d867cd`**, specifically **`git diff 48c10cc..2c7e337`**. Two `git fetch origin` checks confirmed `HEAD = origin/main = 2c7e337`; no extra code required review. Sole independent reviewer: **`openai/gpt-6-astra`**, provider **openai**, verified using this session's runtime metadata and assistant-history provider/model fields. No delegation, substitute model, dependency download, paid compute, commit or push.
+
+**The 7734 file-durability defect is fixed.** Every retained reset/replay matrix passes, including the expanded **388-case** current intent matrix; **840 tests pass**, full suite exactly once. The remaining gate issue is a newly witnessed, pre-existing **Medium startup artifact-preservation gap**: `_read_anchor()` still equates an `open()` ENOENT with absence of the anchor directory entry. With a missing journal and dangling `.id` symlink, ordinary construction silently replaces the existing anchor entry and declares a fresh journal healthy, contrary to the stated “neither exists / damaged storage fences” contract. This is **not** evidence of authorization resurrection. The 7734 diagnostic finding also has a **Low residual**: the failure fence has `presence_error`, but its corresponding `journal_resets` audit entry does not.
+
+Evidence: [index](../experiments/20261008-astra-7741/README.md), [ledger](../experiments/20261008-astra-7741/RUN.md), [retained reset matrix](../experiments/20261008-astra-7741/reset7727.json), [intent matrix](../experiments/20261008-astra-7741/intent7734.json), [independent strict-check/race/metadata witnesses](../experiments/20261008-astra-7741/focused7741.json). Exactly pinned source was exported to `/tmp/hive-astra-7741-source`; historical evidence is a read-only-use `experiments` link. Production files, tests and `scratch/` were not modified.
+
+## Findings
+
+| Finding | Status / severity | Evidence and scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| F-reset-interruption-replays-restored-pair (7718) | **CLOSED — Medium, established-intent scope** | 208 interruptions: 188 fenced restarts, 12 healthy new-pair/held restarts, eight unchanged-old-pair restarts before confirmation. No discarded replay after confirmed intent. |
+| F-reset-error-live-pending (7718) | **CLOSED — Medium** | 104 caught-error recoveries leave pending empty and live fenced; clearance carries zero rebinds. Retained 96 retry/live-error cases pass. |
+| F-reset-intent-durability-status (7727/7734) | **CLOSED — Medium** | Error-propagating lstat, regular-file check, O_NOFOLLOW, fstat same-device/inode/type check, file fsync then directory fsync. Original witnesses, classification EIO/EACCES, fstat failures and Linux swap probes pass. |
